232:It looks like this person must be Soumu, the boss of Raven.
233:Shijukara sneers disdainfully beside me then walks up to the man with his back to us and speaks to him in a low voice.
234:{character:Shijukara}Boss, Countless Springs referred these two people to us.
235:The moment he hears the words Countless Springs, he turns his head and glances at us out of the corner of his eye. After that, he turns his head back and continues to play mahjong. After one turn, just as Ciri's patience is about to run out, he finally says something to us.
236:Soumu
237:{character:Soumu}People from Countless Springs? Did you just come here to sit quietly and say nothing?
238:Hmm... It looks like it'll be difficult to get along with this man. While I'm still thinking of a tactful way to ask my question, Ciri speaks fearlessly.
239:{character:Ciri}Are you behind the recent wildlife trafficking in One Han City?
240:She really is a superwoman.
241:Soumu sucks hard on the cigarette between his fingers, then speaks sarcastically after exhaling the smoke.
242:{character:Soumu}Raven isn't that short of money yet. There are so many businesses for me to choose from every day. I might even end up with the police on my back if I go to such lengths to capture some animals... Haha, are you stupid, or do you think I'm stupid?
243:{character:Soumu}3 Pin... Didn't you guys eat anything before shuffling the tiles?
244:Standing on my tiptoes, I glance at the discarded tiles in front of Soumu. He played a 3 Pin tile in 3 consecutive turns. His tile luck is quite amazing.
245:Ciri naturally doesn't believe what he's saying. She snorts coldly and has already started reaching for the whip on her waist. I quickly grab her hand.
246:{character:player}Let me take care of this.
247:{character:Soumu}3 Pin...
248:I take a small step forward, but then I step back quickly after hearing that he played a 3 Pin. This distance is safer after all.
249:I quickly explain the events of the other day and share what Kurone Toujou told us to Soumu.
250:Although I deliberately omit the part where Ciri beat up Shijukara and the others, Soumu sneers. Damn, I think I said the wrong thing.
251:{character:Soumu}So you're the ones who beat them up the other day.
252:He doesn't look back at us when he says this, so I don't know what expression he is making and can't tell if he mentioned this because he is thinking of getting revenge for Shijukara.
253:Clap--Clap--Clap-- While I'm still thinking of an explanation, Soumu puts down the mahjong tile in his hand and starts clapping.
254:{character:Soumu}Good job.
255:{character:player}Huh?
256:I watch with surprise as Soumu turns around and suddenly kicks Shijukara next to me fiercely.
257:Shijukara rolls all the way to the sofa on the other side of the room and only manages to stabilize himself after grabbing a handrail while kneeling on the ground, which shows that the kick is just as powerful as Ciri's whip lash the other day.
258:{character:Soumu}I've been too busy dealing with business matters recently, so I haven't had time to train these trash. If you didn't make them realize that they are useless...
259:{character:Soumu}Hah! If they keep degenerating like this, how can I expect these trash to fight bravely for me?
260:I want to remind him that there are many peaceful ways to resolve disputes in modern society, but I choose to keep my mouth closed after seeing the shape of his pectoral muscles under his tight clothes and his massive fists.
261:Even if Ciri can beat Shijukara, it doesn't mean she can beat Soumu. It's completely unnecessary to start a conflict.
262:Soumu lights up another cigarette and blows a few smoke rings in the air slowly before he seems to have made a decision.
263:{character:Soumu}I can't turn a blind eye to it since this happened on our turf. Come here at this time tomorrow, and I'll give you an answer.
264:Ciri and I exchange a glance. This outcome is already a lot better than we expected, so there's no reason to not accept it.
265:{character:player}Okay, thank you.
266:Soumu looks at Shijukara, then Shijukara limps over to Ciri and me and leads us back out from the way we came.
267:At the same time, we hear Soumu's threatening voice behind us...
268:{character:Soumu}If the next tile is also a 6 Sou, I'll make all of you into mahjong tiles.
269:On our way to the exit, we pass by a shrine against the wall that is located on the north side of the building, and several people are praying there in silence. I've never seen this type of shrine in any of the mahjong dojos I've been to, so I can't help feeling a little curious.
270:{character:player}Who do you worship at this shrine?
271:{character:Shijukara}Who else would you worship at a mahjong dojo? The priest of Mahjong Soul Shrine, of course.
272:{character:player}Eh? Why would it be... the priest of Mahjong Soul Shrine? Is it because he controls the mahjong force?
273:After talking to Shijukara all this time, his speaking habits are starting to rub off on me.
274:{character:Shijukara}How would I know? This shrine is in all our Raven hideouts, so we pray to it whenever we have time.
275:{character:Shijukara}In our line of business, it's good to worship a few more gods. A lot of people have been saying recently that the Mahjong Soul Shrine tournament is starting again soon, so everyone has been worshipping it more diligently.
276:Suddenly, he stops walking and also makes me stop. After there's some distance between Ciri and us, he lowers his head and whispers to me mysteriously.
277:{character:Shijukara}Since you helped me stop that ferocious woman yesterday, I'll tell you a secret.
278:{character:Shijukara}We're the ones who spread the rumor about the Mahjong Soul Shrine tournament starting again soon. The lady from Countless Springs told our boss, and our boss told us. We were then told to spread the news.
279:{character:player}Why would you do that? If you're the only ones who know... about this, then wouldn't you have fewer competitors?
280:{character:Shijukara}Do you think you would be worthy of talking to me like this here if I could guess what the boss is thinking?
281:Although I came here to ask about the red-crowned crane, I seemed to have learned something even more incredible. I recall what Saturne said earlier about a certain person receiving word about the competition and presume he heard the news Shijukara and the others had spread.
282:Shijukara makes a throat-slitting gesture.
283:{character:Shijukara}You must not tell anyone this secret... Do you understand?
284:I nod furiously. In fact, I don't think anyone will believe me even if I tell them...
285:Shijukara returns after guiding me to the exit. Ciri is waiting for me at the entrance by the time I walk outside the dojo. Mojito is pacing back and forth around her, and its impatient look reminds me of Soumu, which makes me regret leaving it at the entrance when we went inside.
286:If we brought Mojito inside, maybe they would have a fight?
287:This reminds me of a question that has been circulating on the Internet: "Which one is more powerful, a tiger or a XXX?" For example, the question: "Which one is more powerful, a lion or a tiger?" has been around since I was a child, and people are still debating it even now.
288:Should I ask Ciri this question?
289:There's no better time to ask her than now. Of course I'll ask her now.
290:{character:player}Ciri, can I ask you something?
291:{character:Ciri}What is it?
292:{character:player}Is a black panther or a tiger more powerful?
293:{character:Ciri}...
294:{character:Ciri}You have a brain... Why don't you use it?
295:{character:player}Sorry.
296:It's the Internet's fault.
297:I feel like the moment I ask this question, the surface of my brain will become smoother than usual.
298:I better not ask that question, or else Ciri might think I'm an idiot.
299:It's still early when Ciri and I part ways, so I stop at a mahjong dojo on the way back to play some games.
300:Before I start, I check my mobile phone and see six unread text messages from Nana Shiraishi. Excellent.
301:I turn off the screen and happily play mahjong for the rest of the day.
302:Persuade Ciri to take Mojito somewhere else.
303:Convince the staff that Mojito won't harm anyone.
304:Personally demonstrate how they can pet Mojito.
305:Ask Ciri for help.
306:Have the same idea as Ciri.
307:Have a different idea to Ciri.
308:
309:Ask her because human curiosity knows no bounds.
310:Forget it, it seems stupid.
